RESUME SKILL GAP ANALYZER - UI Design Documentation
================================================================

1. IMPLEMENTATION STEPS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The UI was implemented as a single-page application with four main views:

Step 1: Login Page
    - Email and password authentication form
    - "Register" navigation link for new users
    - Neon-styled card layout with gradient effects

Step 2: Register Page
    - Full name, email, password fields
    - Account creation form
    - Link back to login for existing users

Step 3: Dashboard Page
    - Resume upload area with drag-and-drop support
    - Job category dropdown with all 14 categories
    - Dynamic skill tags generation based on selection
    - Analyze button to process resume

Step 4: Result Page
    - Circular score visualization with animation
    - Progress bars for 4 skill categories
    - Recommendation cards with priority tags


2. LOGIC USED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Navigation Logic:
    - Single page application using display:none/show
    - Each page has unique ID, activated via JavaScript
    - Smooth fade-in animations on page transition

Category-Skills Mapping:
    - 14 job categories stored in JavaScript object
    - Each category has 10 specific skills
    - Skills rendered dynamically when category selected

File Upload Logic:
    - Hidden file input triggered by click
    - Drag-and-drop event listeners added
    - File name displayed on successful upload

Score Calculation:
    - CSS conic-gradient for circular progress
    - --score CSS variable controls fill percentage
    - Progress bar width controlled via style properties


3. TECHNOLOGIES APPLIED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Frontend:
    - HTML5 for semantic structure
    - CSS3 for styling (variables, gradients, animations)
    - Vanilla JavaScript for interactivity
    - Google Fonts (Inter) for typography

Design Elements:
    - CSS custom properties (variables) for theming
    - Grid and Flexbox layouts
    - CSS animations (@keyframes)
    - Hover effects and transitions
    - Backdrop filters

Key Features:
    - NEON color theme with cyan and purple accents
    - DARK background (#0a0a0f)
    - Card-based dashboard layout
    - Modern sans-serif typography (Inter)


4. ASSUMPTIONS MADE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Target Users: IT professionals seeking career guidance
2. Browser Support: Modern browsers with CSS3 and ES6
3. File Formats: PDF and DOCX for resume upload
4. File Size: Maximum 5MB
5. Mobile Responsive: Basic support via media queries
6. No Backend: Frontend-only demonstration
7. Single Session: No persistent login state
8. Static Categories: 14 predefined job categories


5. COMPONENT STRUCTURE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Color Palette:
    - Primary Background: #0a0a0f
    - Card Background: #15151f
    - Neon Cyan (Primary): #00f5ff
    - Neon Purple (Accent): #bf00ff
    - Text Primary: #ffffff
    - Text Secondary: #a0a0b0
    - Border: #252535

Main Components:
    - Page Container (4 pages)
    - Auth Card (login/register)
    - Dashboard Card (upload + selection)
    - Upload Area (drag-drop)
    - Category Select (dropdown)
    - Skill Tags (selectable)
    - Score Circle (visualization)
    - Progress Bars (4 categories)
    - Recommendation Cards (3 cards)


6. FILE STRUCTURE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
index.html - Complete UI implementation
    - Inline CSS in <style> tag
    - Inline JavaScript in <script> tag
    - No external dependencies except Google Fonts


7. HOW TO USE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Open index.html in a modern web browser
2. Navigate between Login/Register pages
3. Select a job category from dropdown
4. View and select relevant skills
5. Click "Analyze Resume" to see results
6. Review score and recommendations
7. Click "New Analysis" to start over


8. CUSTOMIZATION OPTIONS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
To modify colors, change CSS variables in :root:
    --neon-cyan: #00f5ff; (change to any color)
    --neon-purple: #bf00ff;

To add new categories, add to categorySkills object in JavaScript

To modify animations, adjust @keyframes definitions

To change fonts, update Google Fonts import URL


9. LIMITATIONS & FUTURE IMPROVEMENTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Current:
    - Static sample data only
    - No actual resume parsing
    - No backend integration
    - Basic mobile responsive

Recommended Enhancements:
    - PDF parsing with PDF.js
    - Resume text extraction
    - AI-powered skill matching
    - User accounts database
    - History tracking
    - PDF export functionality
    - More detailed analytics
    - Social sharing options


